BEGIN;

UPDATE grammar_chapters SET
  title = 'Articles (A, An, The) & Noun Types',
  position = 3,
  estimated_min = 30,
  difficulty = 2,
  band_target = 'Band 6 accuracy',
  summary = 'Stop guessing a/an/the. Learn the decision path for countable, uncountable, specific, and general nouns that examiners notice on the first page.',
  content = $content${"version": 1, "blocks": [{"id": "b01", "type": "paragraph", "text": "If you fix only one chapter in this whole book, fix this one. Articles are the single highest-error area for learners whose first language does not have them, and Bangla, Hindi, Urdu, and Nepali all lack a direct equivalent of a / an / the. Article errors are the number one reason that otherwise strong Band 7 candidates stay stuck at Band 6.0, because the mistakes are frequent, they appear in almost every sentence, and your ear cannot catch them: your first language never trained it to."}, {"id": "b02", "type": "paragraph", "text": "The comforting news is that a small set of rules covers the great majority of cases, and articles depend heavily on one prior idea -- whether a noun is countable or uncountable -- so we start there."}, {"id": "b03", "type": "heading", "level": 2, "text": "3.1 First, countable versus uncountable nouns"}, {"id": "b04", "type": "paragraph", "text": "Whether you can use a / an at all depends on this distinction, so learn it before the article rules. Countable nouns can be counted and have a plural form: one book, two books; a student, five students. They can take a / an in the singular. Uncountable nouns are treated as a single mass and have no plural form and no a / an: information (never informations), water, advice."}, {"id": "b05", "type": "callout", "variant": "warning", "title": "High-frequency uncountable nouns", "text": "Memorise as a fixed block: information, advice, knowledge, research, equipment, furniture, accommodation, traffic, progress, news, money, water, work, luggage, baggage, software, staff, homework, feedback, transport, machinery, vocabulary."}, {"id": "b06", "type": "table", "headers": ["Wrong", "Right"], "rows": [["an advice", "a piece of advice / some advice"], ["an information", "a piece of information / some information"], ["a research", "a study / a piece of research"], ["a furniture", "a piece of furniture / an item of furniture"], ["a luggage", "a piece of luggage"]]}, {"id": "b07", "type": "heading", "level": 2, "text": "3.2 The three article choices"}, {"id": "b08", "type": "paragraph", "text": "English has three choices for any noun phrase: a / an, the, or the zero article (no article)."}, {"id": "b09", "type": "heading", "level": 3, "text": "a / an (indefinite)"}, {"id": "b10", "type": "paragraph", "text": "Use a / an for a singular countable noun that is not specific -- first mention, one of many, or a job/role: She is an engineer. I read an interesting article. Choose a before a consonant sound and an before a vowel sound: a university (yoo-), an hour (silent h), an honest lawyer."}, {"id": "b11", "type": "heading", "level": 3, "text": "the (definite)"}, {"id": "b12", "type": "paragraph", "text": "Use the when the listener/reader can identify which one you mean: There is only one of it (the sun, the government, the internet, the environment); it is made specific by the words around it (the number of cars, the capital of Bangladesh); with superlatives and ordinals (the highest figure, the first step)."}, {"id": "b13", "type": "heading", "level": 3, "text": "Zero article (no article)"}, {"id": "b14", "type": "paragraph", "text": "Use no article for: plural countable nouns talked about in general (Books are expensive); uncountable nouns talked about in general (Education matters; Water is essential); most proper nouns -- countries, cities, people, languages (Bangladesh, Dhaka, English)."}, {"id": "b15", "type": "heading", "level": 2, "text": "3.3 The decision process (use this when you proofread)"}, {"id": "b16", "type": "paragraph", "text": "When you check any singular noun, run these questions in order: (1) Is it countable? If no (uncountable), you cannot use a / an -- choose the (if specific) or zero article (if general). (2) If yes (countable): is it specific, known, or unique? If yes, use the. (3) If it is not specific and singular: use a / an (by sound). (4) If it is a general plural: use the zero article."}, {"id": "b17", "type": "heading", "level": 2, "text": "3.4 Fixed cases worth memorising"}, {"id": "b18", "type": "paragraph", "text": "Some article choices are fixed: the internet, the environment, the economy, the government, the media, the public, the world take the. Superlatives always take the. Institutions used for their purpose take zero article (go to school, go to university, at home) -- add the only for the specific building. Most countries take zero article; plural or united/republic names take the (the United States, the United Kingdom). First mention a, second mention the: The chart shows a sharp rise in 2018. The rise continued into 2019."}, {"id": "b19", "type": "l1_error_fixer", "title": "Why Bangla speakers misuse articles", "body": "Because Bangla has no articles at all, the category does not exist in your mental grammar, so it must be learned as an English-only system rather than translated. Three error patterns dominate.", "error_types": [{"label": "Omitting \"the\" for specific and unique things", "incorrect": "Internet has changed our lives. / Government should fund school.", "correct": "The internet has changed our lives. / The government should fund schools."}, {"label": "Using \"a / an\" with uncountable nouns", "incorrect": "He gave me an advice. / She did a research on it.", "correct": "He gave me some advice / a piece of advice. / She did research / a study on it."}, {"label": "Dropping the article before a singular countable noun", "incorrect": "Government should take step to reduce pollution.", "correct": "The government should take steps to reduce pollution."}]}, {"id": "b20", "type": "ielts_impact", "skills": ["writing", "speaking"], "title": "The number one Band 6 ceiling", "body": "Article control is audited densely across every task. In Task 1 a single sentence can require three separate article decisions. Because the errors are so frequent, they are the classic thing separating a script that reads like Band 7 in ideas but scores Band 6 in Grammatical Range and Accuracy. Consistent article control is one of the clearest Band 6.5-plus signals you can send.", "examples": {"task1": "The graph illustrates the proportion of households with an internet connection.", "task2": "Education is widely seen as the key to development, and governments should therefore fund schools properly.", "speaking": "The person who influenced me most was a teacher at my primary school."}}]}$content$::jsonb,
  is_published = true,
  updated_at = now()
WHERE slug = 'ch3-articles-nouns';

INSERT INTO grammar_exercises (id, chapter_id, slug, title, kind, instructions, items, position, is_published)
VALUES (
  'a1000001-0001-4000-8000-000000000231',
  'a1000001-0001-4000-8000-000000000103',
  'ex-3-1-article-insertion',
  'Exercise 3.1 - Article Insertion',
  'correction',
  'Rewrite each sentence inserting a, an, or the where needed. Some blanks need the zero article (no word); mark those with (0).',
  $items1$[{"id": "q1", "prompt": "___ education is ___ key to ___ economic development.", "answer": "(0) Education is the key to (0) economic development.", "accepted": ["Education is the key to economic development.", "(0) Education is the key to (0) economic development."], "reason": "General uncountable education and economic development = zero; the key = unique role.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q2", "prompt": "She is ___ most hard-working student in ___ class.", "answer": "She is the most hard-working student in the class.", "accepted": ["She is the most hard-working student in the class."], "reason": "Superlative needs the; the class is specific.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q3", "prompt": "___ chart shows ___ number of tourists visiting ___ museum.", "answer": "The chart shows the number of tourists visiting the museum.", "accepted": ["The chart shows the number of tourists visiting the museum.", "The chart shows the number of tourists visiting a museum."], "reason": "Specific chart and number; museum often the/a depending on context.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q4", "prompt": "___ internet has transformed ___ way people communicate.", "answer": "The internet has transformed the way people communicate.", "accepted": ["The internet has transformed the way people communicate."], "reason": "the internet is unique; the way is specific.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q5", "prompt": "He wants to become ___ honest lawyer after ___ university.", "answer": "He wants to become an honest lawyer after (0) university.", "accepted": ["He wants to become an honest lawyer after university.", "He wants to become an honest lawyer after (0) university."], "reason": "an before vowel sound; go to university = zero article for purpose.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q6", "prompt": "___ pollution is ___ serious problem in ___ major cities.", "answer": "(0) Pollution is a serious problem in (0) major cities.", "accepted": ["Pollution is a serious problem in major cities.", "(0) Pollution is a serious problem in (0) major cities."], "reason": "General uncountable; a for singular countable first mention; general plural zero.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q7", "prompt": "I read ___ interesting article yesterday. ___ article was about ___ climate change.", "answer": "I read an interesting article yesterday. The article was about (0) climate change.", "accepted": ["I read an interesting article yesterday. The article was about climate change."], "reason": "First mention a/an, second the; general uncountable climate change = zero.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q8", "prompt": "___ government should invest more in ___ public transport.", "answer": "The government should invest more in (0) public transport.", "accepted": ["The government should invest more in public transport."], "reason": "the government unique; public transport general uncountable.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q9", "prompt": "___ United States and ___ United Kingdom signed ___ agreement.", "answer": "The United States and the United Kingdom signed an agreement.", "accepted": ["The United States and the United Kingdom signed an agreement."], "reason": "Plural/united country names take the; an agreement first mention.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q10", "prompt": "___ sun rises in ___ east.", "answer": "The sun rises in the east.", "accepted": ["The sun rises in the east."], "reason": "Unique sun and fixed the east.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q11", "prompt": "___ poverty remains ___ obstacle to ___ progress in ___ developing world.", "answer": "(0) Poverty remains an obstacle to (0) progress in the developing world.", "accepted": ["Poverty remains an obstacle to progress in the developing world."], "reason": "General uncountables zero; an obstacle; the developing world specific.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q12", "prompt": "She gave me ___ useful advice about ___ visa process.", "answer": "She gave me (0) useful advice about the visa process.", "accepted": ["She gave me useful advice about the visa process.", "She gave me some useful advice about the visa process."], "reason": "advice uncountable - no a; the visa process specific.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q13", "prompt": "___ number of ___ students who fail ___ exam is rising.", "answer": "The number of (0) students who fail the exam is rising.", "accepted": ["The number of students who fail the exam is rising."], "reason": "the number of is fixed; students general; the exam specific context.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q14", "prompt": "My brother is ___ engineer, and he works for ___ large company.", "answer": "My brother is an engineer, and he works for a large company.", "accepted": ["My brother is an engineer, and he works for a large company."], "reason": "Job and first-mention singular countable take a/an.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q15", "prompt": "___ water is essential for ___ life on ___ Earth.", "answer": "(0) Water is essential for (0) life on (0) Earth. / the Earth.", "accepted": ["Water is essential for life on Earth.", "Water is essential for life on the Earth."], "reason": "General uncountables zero; Earth often zero or the.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q16", "prompt": "We stayed in ___ hotel near ___ airport; ___ hotel was cheap.", "answer": "We stayed in a hotel near the airport; the hotel was cheap.", "accepted": ["We stayed in a hotel near the airport; the hotel was cheap."], "reason": "First a, second the; the airport specific in context.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q17", "prompt": "___ research shows that ___ exercise improves ___ mental health.", "answer": "(0) Research shows that (0) exercise improves (0) mental health.", "accepted": ["Research shows that exercise improves mental health."], "reason": "All general uncountables = zero article.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q18", "prompt": "___ environment must be protected for ___ future generations.", "answer": "The environment must be protected for (0) future generations.", "accepted": ["The environment must be protected for future generations."], "reason": "the environment unique; general plural zero.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q19", "prompt": "He spent ___ hour reading ___ book about ___ history of ___ Bangladesh.", "answer": "He spent an hour reading a book about the history of (0) Bangladesh.", "accepted": ["He spent an hour reading a book about the history of Bangladesh."], "reason": "an hour (vowel sound); a book first mention; the history of X; country zero.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q20", "prompt": "___ traffic in ___ capital is ___ major source of ___ air pollution.", "answer": "(0) Traffic in the capital is a major source of (0) air pollution.", "accepted": ["Traffic in the capital is a major source of air pollution."], "reason": "traffic/air pollution uncountable general; the capital specific; a major source.", "bn_note": null}]$items1$::jsonb,
  1,
  true
)
ON CONFLICT (chapter_id, slug) DO UPDATE SET
  title = EXCLUDED.title,
